From: mml555 <29288598+mml555@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 16:48:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Route B: Dart SDK support, bytecode producer, and the
 target->pool instrument
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Dart half of the self-hosted Route B toolchain, committed to version control
for the first time. Until now it existed ONLY as uncommitted working-tree edits
in a shallow (depth-1) checkout cloned from a local mirror — no history, no
offsite copy, and no way to rebase onto a future Dart revision.

Base: 6b58bb3a (dart.googlesource.com/sdk)

WHAT IS HERE

  runtime/include/dart_route_b_trace.h    the v5 trace record (NEW). Deliberately
                                          a separate header from dart_api.h
  runtime/lib/object.cc                   Dart_RouteBActivatePatchTraced, the
                                          derived target->pool scan, the demoted
                                          supplied-offset assertion
  runtime/vm/object.{cc,h}                patchable static call support
  runtime/vm/compiler/...                 AOT: call specializer, dispatch table,
                                          precompiler, flow-graph (arm64)
  pkg/dart2bytecode/...                   the bytecode producer
  pkg/front_end/...                       private-name resolution, compiler opts
  sdk/lib/_internal/vm/, sdk/lib/internal internal patches

A NOTE ON SNAPSHOT_HASH, because it governs whether shipped patches keep working

runtime/vm/object.{cc,h} are in VM_SNAPSHOT_FILES, so these edits DO move
SNAPSHOT_HASH away from vanilla Dart. That is fine and is not new: every Route B
cell carries them, which is why the hash is IDENTICAL across cells 80e493e4,
87130ae8, cd137db6 and 50bdae36 (21139db2770724220da55c72db00acdc) — the property
that made the release-91 hybrid measurement admissible at all.

The 0012 instrument was deliberately kept OUT of those files, in
runtime/lib/object.cc, precisely so adding it could not move the hash and break
already-published App snapshots. Anything added here in future must respect the
same boundary.

These are the exact bytes behind every G15 result in selfhost/evidence/g15.

ONE COMMIT, for the same reason as the engine-side commit: the .patch stack
decomposes this logically, but the tree carries it merged, and these are the
bytes with device evidence behind them. A reconstructed decomposition would be
plausible but unbuilt. Future changes get their own commits.

NOT INCLUDED: third_party/binaryen/.DS_Store.

STILL SHALLOW at this commit. `git fetch --unshallow` from
https://dart.googlesource.com/sdk.git is required before this branch can rebase
onto a newer Dart revision — there is no common ancestor to rebase through yet.

